    "explanation": "Rider and driver, this is decided on the driver's own GPS trace. The trip was accepted at 20:22:12 and cancelled by the driver at 20:32:36 under the reason code RIDER_NO_SHOW. The trace EV-GPS-02711 runs from 20:22:14 to 20:33:44 at 10-second sampling, 100% coverage, no gaps, and it never once puts the car inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius for Blk 231 Serangoon Ave 3: the derived arrival block reports qualifying_fix_count = 0 and a longest qualifying in-geofence run of 0.0 seconds, and the closest the car ever came to the pickup pin across the whole trip was 156.99 m. Under POL-NS-02 the three-consecutive-in-radius-fix test is therefore not met, the driver never arrived, POL-NS-01 limb (b) fails, and the rider is entitled to a full refund of the cancellation fee. It makes no difference that the record shows an 'arrived' tap at 20:28:14 and a 4.4-minute wait timer: those are the driver's own status entries, and POL-NS-02 reads position, not the tap. Independently, POL-NS-06 refunds the fee in full: the effective in-geofence dwell is 0.0 seconds against the 180-second free waiting period in force for this trip (trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec = 180), a shortfall of 180 seconds, whether or not the rider was present. The traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-02711-01 is MISSING at weight 0.0, so POL-NS-06 limb (i) is unavailable and the driver cannot accumulate any dwell across separate intervals or excuse the shortfall on kerb-restriction grounds. The arrival marker is also a false one: the trace's recorded speeds are either 0.0 km/h (the final readings, after the 20:32:36 cancellation) or between 33.1 and 62.4 km/h, so at the 20:28:14 marker the car was in motion on the road well above the 15 km/h threshold in POL-NS-05, and there is no in-geofence fix at or before that timestamp; under POL-NS-05 the marker does not start the waiting clock, and because no qualifying in-geofence fix exists anywhere in the trip, POL-NS-05(ii) gives the full refund, no compensation, and the false-arrival record I have placed in the referrals. On the driver's statement 'I was at the pickup as shown on the map': the map is in the record and it shows the opposite, and a statement carries no weight multiplier and cannot satisfy the 50 m test the clause sets. On the rider's contact: her message at 20:28:34 did name her position, but the driver replied 'ok' at 20:29:04, 30 seconds later, so POL-NS-04 limb (b) fails and that clause cannot operate here — her recorded presence (47 fixes, all at 0.0 km/h, a mean of 12.03 m from the pin) is not needed for the refund and does not change it. If this is instead treated as a wrong-face-of-the-pin case under POL-NS-03, the closest approach of 156.99 m is inside the 400 m ceiling, and the same result follows: the rider named the 'main entrance next to the taxi stand, block A' and the driver did not move to it before cancelling, so the driver bears the loss and receives no compensation. Money: EV-FARE-02711 shows cancellation_fee 4.50, total_charged 4.50, payment_status CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd 0.00. The whole SGD 4.50 is refunded to the rider. Driver compensation is nil: POL-NS-07 pays 80% of the fee only where POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full, and it is not, so driver_compensation_sgd is null. Nothing escalates: there is no POL-NS-08 impairment (the trace, trip record, chat log and fare ledger are all COMPLETE at weight 1.0, and the fare line reconciles to the 4.50 net fee), no unresolved contradiction (POL-NS-02 and POL-NS-05 answer the arrival question the driver's statement raises), no profile signal (no_show_terminations_30d 2 against completed_trips_30d 87, a rate of 0.023, below the 4-or-more and 0.08 anti-farming test; no_show_disputes_30d 0; zero disputes with the counterparty on either side), and my confidence rests on artifacts all at weight 1.0, so the cap is 1.0 and I have set 0.95. The refund of 4.50 is below the SGD 8.00 automatic execution threshold and executes on issue. Finally, I have not added a driver-education referral for the mis-selected reason code: POL-NS-01 attaches that referral to a case where the driver's stationary fixes lie inside the arrival radius, and this trace has none. The inconsistency between a RIDER_NO_SHOW code and a rider who was at the pin is noted here as an open question for the reviewer rather than as a referral."
