    "explanation": "Both parties: this ruling concerns the SGD 4.50 no-show cancellation fee on trip TRP-02711. The fee is refunded to the rider in full and the driver receives no compensation. The monetary effect (SGD 4.50) is below the SGD 8.00 automatic execution threshold, so it executes on issue.\n\nWhy the fee does not stand. A no-show fee is chargeable only if all four POL-NS-01 conditions hold; two fail on the recorded evidence. Arrival (limb b): the zone class is STANDARD, so the arrival radius is 50 m (fee_schedule.arrival_radius_m; POL-NS-02). GPS trace EV-GPS-02711 (weight 1.0) never places the driver inside that radius - the derived arrival block reports 0 qualifying in-geofence fixes anywhere in the trip, the longest qualifying run is 0.0 seconds, and the driver's closest recorded approach to the pin is 156.99 m (mean 1,807 m, maximum 6,160 m). Under POL-NS-02 the driver never arrived, and POL-NS-01 limb (b) fails. The driver's statement that he 'was at the pickup as shown on the map' is not supported by his own trace: the closest he came was 157 m. Dwell (limb c): the free waiting period in force is 180 seconds (trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec), the effective in-geofence dwell is 0.0 seconds, a shortfall of 180 seconds, so POL-NS-06 independently makes the fee not chargeable, whether or not the rider was present. The 'arrived' tap at 20:28:14 is a driver-pressed marker (arrival_marker BUTTON), not a platform-confirmed one; it starts no waiting clock the GPS does not support, and POL-NS-12 (GPS_AUTO arrival) does not apply.\n\nNo driver compensation. POL-NS-07 pays the driver only where POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full, and it is not. On the driver's own trace his closest approach (156.99 m) lies outside the 50 m radius but inside the 400 m wrong-entrance ceiling, which is POL-NS-03 territory, and there the chat log allocates the cost: the rider named her position at 20:28:34 ('im at the main entrance next to the taxi stand, block A') and the driver did not move to it before cancelling at 20:32:36, so under POL-NS-03(i) the driver bears the loss and receives nothing. POL-NS-03(ii)'s pin-ambiguity goodwill does not apply: trip_record.registered_pickup_points is 1, not 2 or more, and the rider did name a sub-location. Whichever of POL-NS-02 and POL-NS-03 is taken as the governing route, the money is the same - full refund, no compensation.\n\nThe rider's claims. Her own track (47 of 47 qualifying fixes within 9.1-14.8 m of the pin, stationary, 20:26:34 to 20:33:28) shows she was at the pickup point throughout, which rebuts any suggestion of rider absence. Her POL-NS-04 claim is not the route that decides this case: limb (b) of that clause fails because the driver did reply in the chat within 120 seconds ('ok' at 20:29:04, 30 seconds after her message), so POL-NS-04 cannot exonerate her - but her presence was never in issue, because the fee fails on arrival and dwell on the driver's own evidence.\n\nReferrals: none. The rider asks for a false-arrival record against the driver under POL-NS-05(ii). That limb fires only where the 'arrived' marker is false, and POL-NS-05 tests that by matching the marker's timestamp to a fix more than 300 m from the pin or to motion at 15 km/h or above. The record's closest approach is 156.99 m - well inside 300 m - and POL-NS-05's own terms put a driver stationary within 300 m of the pin but outside the arrival radius under POL-NS-03, not under it; so no false-arrival referral is produced. The driver in turn asks for a driver-education entry under POL-NS-01 for a mis-selected reason code; that referral attaches to the branch where the driver's stationary fixes lie inside the arrival radius, which is not this case (closest 157 m), and RIDER_NO_SHOW is one of the three codes limb (d) recognises. The referrals list is therefore empty. The residual open question for review - whether the driver genuinely stood at the wrong face of the block or simply tapped 'arrived' from the wrong side of the road - changes neither the refund nor the compensation and is recorded here rather than as a referral.\n\nEscalation is not engaged. The anti-farming check does not trip (no_show_terminations_30d 2 against completed_trips_30d 87, a rate of 0.023, against a threshold of 4 or more and above 0.08); there is no repeat-abuse pattern (no_show_disputes_30d 0, disputes_with_counterparty_90d 0 on both sides); the trace has no gaps and a full rider track; the chat matches trip_record.chat_message_count 2 with intact numbering; there is no clock skew (the nearest fix to the 20:28:14 marker is 20:28:14); and the fare line (SGD 4.50, payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.00) reconciles with platform_policy.cancellation_fee_sgd of SGD 4.50, so there is no POL-NS-08 defect.\n\nEvidence and weight. The deciding facts are carried by EV-GPS-02711, EV-TRIP-02711 and EV-FARE-02711, each at weight 1.0, so the POL-GEN-02(2) cap is 1.0 and confidence is 0.95. EV-ADVIS-02711-01 is MISSING, weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT; it carries no fact, and its absence is why POL-NS-06(i) accumulation is unavailable, exactly as the derived arrival block records - so no kerb-restriction excuse for the 180-second shortfall is available to the driver. One claim was discarded by the referee and appears in the audit record below: the driver's advisory claim failed because it cited that MISSING artifact without naming its issue code, as POL-GEN-02(1) requires."
